WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.420 --> 00:00:05.640
- This video describes EQ-RADIO,
a new technology from Professor

00:00:05.640 --> 00:00:09.010
Katabi's group at MIT, that
can recognize people's emotions

00:00:09.010 --> 00:00:11.170
using wireless signals.

00:00:11.170 --> 00:00:14.110
Was there a moment in your life
when you looked at someone's

00:00:14.110 --> 00:00:17.800
face, but you could not
figure out how they feel?

00:00:17.800 --> 00:00:21.710
What if your wireless router
can tell people's emotions,

00:00:21.710 --> 00:00:24.190
even if they don't show
them on their faces?

00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:27.760
This is exactly what
our technology does.

00:00:27.760 --> 00:00:29.460
This is our device.

00:00:29.460 --> 00:00:31.480
The device transmits
a wireless signal

00:00:31.480 --> 00:00:34.390
which reflects off a person's
body, and comes back.

00:00:34.390 --> 00:00:36.790
It captures these
reflections, and analyzes them

00:00:36.790 --> 00:00:38.860
to infer the person's emotions.

00:00:38.860 --> 00:00:40.810
Specifically, our
algorithms zoom in

00:00:40.810 --> 00:00:43.060
on the wireless
reflections to extract

00:00:43.060 --> 00:00:46.300
the minute variations due
to breathing, and heartbeat.

00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:48.520
We then further analyze
these reflections

00:00:48.520 --> 00:00:51.820
to extract the breathing signal,
and the heart beat signal.

00:00:51.820 --> 00:00:53.560
We then zoom in more
on these signals

00:00:53.560 --> 00:00:57.040
to obtain individual heartbeat,
and breathing cycles,

00:00:57.040 --> 00:01:00.220
and feed these as features into
a machine learning algorithm

00:01:00.220 --> 00:01:02.260
to recognize that
person's emotions.

00:01:02.260 --> 00:01:03.700
The device can
automatically know

00:01:03.700 --> 00:01:07.730
if the person is excited,
angry, sad, or happy.

00:01:07.730 --> 00:01:09.700
Our device can
recognize emotions

00:01:09.700 --> 00:01:13.870
with an accuracy of 87%, while
relying purely on wireless

00:01:13.870 --> 00:01:15.130
signals.

00:01:15.130 --> 00:01:18.760
We envision that EQ-Radio can
be used in many applications.

00:01:18.760 --> 00:01:20.830
It can recognize the
person's emotions

00:01:20.830 --> 00:01:23.770
while he is watching a movie,
and provide movie makers

00:01:23.770 --> 00:01:26.780
with better tools to
evaluate user experience.

00:01:26.780 --> 00:01:28.660
It can also allow
smart environments

00:01:28.660 --> 00:01:31.450
to detect emotional
states like depression,

00:01:31.450 --> 00:01:35.590
and inform us to improve
our emotional well-being.

00:01:35.590 --> 00:01:37.870
It can even enable
these environments

00:01:37.870 --> 00:01:41.000
to react to our moods, and
adjust lighting or music

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:41.740
accordingly.

00:01:46.520 --> 00:01:48.590
To learn more about
this research, please

00:01:48.590 --> 00:01:50.880
check out our website.

